
---

📚 Springboot-LMS-EKS – CI with Jenkins & CD with ArgoCD

🚀 Project Overview

This project implements a CI/CD pipeline for a Spring Boot Library Management System deployed on AWS EKS.

CI (Continuous Integration) → Jenkins master-slave architecture
CD (Continuous Deployment) → ArgoCD (GitOps)

It integrates: Terraform, Ansible, Nexus, SonarQube, Docker, Helm, EFK, Prometheus, Grafana for a complete DevOps ecosystem.

---

🏗️ Jenkins Master-Slave Setup

🖥 Master Node

   Orchestrates CI pipeline
   Runs Terraform (AWS infra provisioning)
   Runs Ansible (agent & service configuration)

 🛠 Build Agent → Builds Spring Boot app with Maven

 📦 Nexus Agent → Uploads artifacts to Nexus Repository

 🐳 Docker Agent → Builds & pushes Docker images (ECR & DockerHub)

 🔍 Sonar Agent → Runs SonarQube analysis

 ☸ Automation Host (EKS Agent) → Handles infra tasks, but final deployment is handled by ArgoCD

---

 🔄 CI Pipeline (Jenkins)

1️⃣ Checkout (Master) → Pulls code from GitHub, stashes for agents
2️⃣ Provision & Configure (Master) → Terraform + Ansible for infra and services
3️⃣ Code Quality (Sonar Agent) → Static analysis with SonarQube
4️⃣ Build (Build Agent) → Builds Spring Boot JAR with Maven
5️⃣ Artifact Upload (Nexus Agent) → Stores JAR in Nexus Repository
6️⃣ Docker Build & Push (Docker Agent) → Builds Docker image, pushes to ECR & DockerHub

📌 End of CI → The new Docker image tag is committed to Git → ArgoCD picks up for deployment.

---

 🔄 CD Pipeline (ArgoCD – GitOps)

 Helm charts & manifests are versioned in GitHub
 ArgoCD watches the repo for changes
 On update (new image tag), ArgoCD:

   Syncs manifests
   Deploys app to EKS cluster
 Benefits:

   Automated, Declarative, Rollback-friendly

---

 📊 Monitoring & Logging

 EFK Stack (Elasticsearch, Fluentd, Kibana) → Logging
 Prometheus & Grafana → Metrics & dashboards

---

