        └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

🔄 CI/CD Pipeline Flow

CI - Jenkins

GitHub → Jenkins → Maven Build → Docker Build → Push to Registry

CD - ArgoCD

ArgoCD watches GitOps repo → detects Helm/K8s changes → deploys to EKS

Infra

Terraform provisions infra

Ansible configures nodes & installs dependencies

---

 ⚙️ Tech Stack

 CI: Jenkins (Master + Agents)
 CD: ArgoCD (GitOps)
 Infra: Terraform, Ansible, AWS EKS
 Code Quality: SonarQube
 Artifacts: Nexus Repository
 Containers: Docker, AWS ECR, DockerHub
 Deployment: Helm, ArgoCD
 Monitoring: Prometheus, Grafana
 Logging: EFK Stack

---

 📂 Repository Structure

```bash
Springboot-LMS-EKS/
├── .github/                     # GitHub Actions (optional workflows)
│   └── workflows/
├── .mvn/                        # Maven wrapper
│   └── wrapper/
├── ansible/                     # Ansible playbooks for configuration
│   ├── inventory/               # Inventory of hosts
│   └── roles/                   # Roles for each agent/service
│       ├── build_agent/
│       ├── docker/
│       ├── eks_automation_setup/
│       ├── jenkins/
│       ├── nexus/
│       └── sonarqube/
├── helm-k8-service/             # Helm charts for Kubernetes deployment
│   ├── frontend/
│   └── user-service/
├── spare/                       # Backup/extra configs
├── src/                         # Spring Boot application source code
│   ├── main/java/com/java/      # App code (controllers, services, repos, etc.)
│   ├── main/resources/          # Resources (templates, configs)
│   └── test/java/com/java/      # Unit & integration tests
├── target/                      # Build output (generated by Maven)
├── terraform/                   # Terraform IaC
│   ├── environments/            # Environments (dev, prod)
│   └── modules/                 # Reusable modules (ec2, eks, network, rds)
└── Jenkinsfile                  # CI pipeline definition
```

---

 🚦 Workflow

1. Developer Commit → GitHub
2. CI (Jenkins Master + Agents)

    Terraform + Ansible (infra, config)
    Code analysis → Build → Artifact → Docker image push
3. CD (ArgoCD)

    GitOps syncs Helm manifests to EKS
4. Observability

    Logs in Kibana
    Metrics in Grafana

---

 📌 Future Enhancements

 ✅ Blue/Green or Canary deployments with ArgoCD
 ✅ Auto-scaling (HPA) for user-service
 ✅ Secret management with HashiCorp Vault / AWS SSM
 ✅ Alerts via Prometheus Alertmanager

